cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  foldrunner: all-vs-all structure-prediction panels with one
  alignment per sequence
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jiajun
    family-names: Li
    email: ChiaChun.Le@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/ChiaChunL/foldrunner
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  foldrunner turns a protein library into structure-prediction jobs. It
  enumerates all-vs-all pairs including self-pairs, computes each multiple
  sequence alignment once and addresses it by sequence content, and writes
  native input files for AlphaFold 3, AlphaFold Server, Boltz-2, Protenix,
  Chai-1, ColabFold, AlphaFold2-Multimer and SeedFold. Paired and unpaired
  alignments are kept apart and the paired depth is reported per job, because
  cross-species pairs have almost no pairing and their interface scores are
  therefore not comparable to same-species pairs.
keywords:
  - alphafold
  - structure-prediction
  - protein-protein-interaction
  - multiple-sequence-alignment
  - bioinformatics
references:
  - type: software
    title: >-
      foldmetrics: unified confidence metrics and interface contacts for
      structure-prediction models
    authors:
      - given-names: Jiajun
        family-names: Li
    repository-code: https://github.com/ChiaChunL/foldmetrics
    license: BSD-3-Clause
    notes: >-
      Reads the outputs foldrunner's panels produce and computes ipSAE, pDockQ2,
      LIS and DockQ across engines.
